package icons

// Slack's file-type SvgIcons (D0WB's FileEntityIcon map and the file
// surfaces' own icons; icons.json from slack-datamine-plus's build), that
// the set lacked: the brand glyphs (Adobe, Android, Apple, Dropbox Paper,
// Lucid, Markdown, Microsoft Office, Zoho), database, disc-image, gauge,
// media-archive, pdf-file, presentation, quip, text, three-d-graphic and
// zip; and the outline binary, document, gauge, pdf-file and transcript
// that getFileTypeSvgIconName names, which search's type filter and
// rich_text file slugs draw. Redrawn on the 20-unit grid the way the set's
// others are: a solid glyph as fl parts (Slack's region, evenodd or nonzero
// as its path says, nonzero face by face, so a piece wound against the
// largest ring still fills: the Ai's dot, the apple's leaf; inset by half
// its band, each piece's band the widest whose inset keeps the piece's
// parts and holes (the Android's eyes enclosed, the Id's d bowl joined to
// its stem) and fits within 0.005 of the best, so sharp tips keep more of
// themselves (markdown's arrow, Excel's X, Word's W, Dropbox Paper's
// corners); swf's letters at 0.5, a core no thinner than its band), line
// art as one s part on its 1.5-unit walls' centrelines (the medial axis,
// its junctions and corners put back where the walls' lines cross, round
// loops as circle(), a dot as disc(), what the strokes leave, a junction
// where walls merge or a hub, filled on its own), each wall stroked once:
// stroking both sides of an inset sliver inks every edge twice, 11-43%
// heavy (icon-shots 45369119745). Each matches its Slack outline at IoU >=
// 0.97 (the redrawn parts re-expanded by their bands); TestIconsMatchSlack
// holds their ink.
